{"id":"sh/u1k3idsz","text":"01 / THE MODEL","position":{"left":78,"top":28,"width":1100,"height":28},"style":{"fontSize":18,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#637176","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"id":"sh/v2t4bi9k","text":"A duty is one bus. The economic choice is the whole fleet.","position":{"left":78,"top":78,"width":1120,"height":108},"style":{"fontSize":42,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#102B36","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"id":"tb/98jad8za","text":"Object\tMeaning\nService\tMandatory trip with timing and energy use\nDuty\tOne bus's services, movements and charging\nComplete plan x\tAll duties, jointly feasible under shared resources\ne(x), c(x)\tGrid energy by interval and fleet operating cost","position":{"left":80,"top":208,"width":1120,"height":310}}
{"id":"sh/58vmhsrm","text":"Shared plugs and service coverage belong inside feasibility. Public and learning experiments are charge-only; V2G results use ideal analytical models.","position":{"left":80,"top":576,"width":1120,"height":95},"style":{"fontSize":27,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#315A63","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
