{"id":"sh/7qhc3edo","text":"Supply cost, a posted bill and strategic payment differ.","position":{"left":78,"top":78,"width":1120,"height":108},"style":{"fontSize":42,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#102B36","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"id":"tb/jiponu9s","text":"Decision\tObjective\tWhat changes during a deviation?\nPlanner\tc(x) + F(e(x))\tSupply cost follows the load\nPosted-price fleet\tc(x) + p · e(x)\tThe announced price p stays fixed\nStrategic fleet\tc(x) + p(e(x)) · e(x)\tPrice responds under a specified rule","position":{"left":80,"top":208,"width":1120,"height":310}}
{"id":"sh/5oza14vi","text":"A support test asks whether the planner's choice also minimizes the fixed-price bill.","position":{"left":80,"top":576,"width":1120,"height":95},"style":{"fontSize":27,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#315A63","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
