{"id":"sh/ihgb6xsj","text":"Charging flexibility and vehicle fees jointly determine support.","position":{"left":78,"top":78,"width":1120,"height":108},"style":{"fontSize":42,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#102B36","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"id":"sh/lo3ap8rq","text":"Terminal power K and fee f","position":{"left":80,"top":205,"width":520,"height":70},"style":{"fontSize":28,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#315A63","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"id":"sh/0nu9w3al","text":"For 20 < K ≤ 30:\nl = 30 − K, d = K − 20.\n\nGap > 0 exactly when\nmax(0, 2d(l − 5)/5) < f < 2d.","position":{"left":80,"top":290,"width":520,"height":250},"style":{"fontSize":27,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#102B36","alignment":"left"}}
{"id":"sh/s7axwri1","text":"How to read it","position":{"left":655,"top":205,"width":520,"height":70},"style":{"fontSize":28,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#315A63","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"id":"sh/d8je5wjm","text":"More charging flexibility can introduce unsupported choices while lowering physical system cost.\n\nBoundary, zero-fee and infeasible cases have separate treatment.","position":{"left":655,"top":290,"width":520,"height":250},"style":{"fontSize":27,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#102B36","alignment":"left"}}
{"id":"sh/qlsfuh0v","text":"The proof covers a continuum. Agreement on 20 exact cases checks implementations, not population prevalence.","position":{"left":80,"top":576,"width":1120,"height":95},"style":{"fontSize":27,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#315A63","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
